  "description": "meme-id: free dishwasher; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man loading dishes into a dishwasher while a woman watches, with text overlay reading 'free dishwasher' and 'missing parts'. The overall intent is to humorously highlight the irony or absurdity of receiving something free that is incomplete or defective. The meme uses the visual of a domestic scene to create a relatable, lighthearted commentary on consumer experiences, specifically the frustration of getting a free item that lacks necessary components. There is no toxicity, hate, or harmful intent toward any specific group; it is a benign, situational joke. The 'missing parts' text serves as the punchline, implying the 'free' offer is a trap or a scam, which is a common trope in internet humor. The meme does not target any protected characteristic or community and is not abusive, cyberbullying, or propagandistic. It is intended to be funny and relatable, not harmful.",
